"""Editorial questions for brain-computer interfaces, virtual worlds, and digital humans."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


BCI = """history_origins|A Neural Interface Milestone|Which experiment first supported a bounded control or communication task?|Use dated study methods and participant outcomes.
famous_examples|A BCI Demonstration Rechecked|What did a participant do independently and under what assistance?|Compare task, calibration, sessions, and limitations.
hidden_stories|Participants and Support Teams|Whose time, care, and maintenance make BCI research possible?|Use consented accounts and study records.
beginner_explainers|Signal to Intentional Action|How does recorded neural activity become a device command?|Trace acquisition, decoding, feedback, and user correction.
advanced_concepts|Decoding Error and User Agency|How does uncertainty in inferred intent affect real communication?|Measure accuracy, error correction, and participant preferences.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Performance Change Across Sessions|Which signal, device, or user factors explain variation?|Compare dated sessions and calibration data.
technology_innovation|A New Neural Interface|Did one design improve a defined task and participant outcome?|Examine nonclinical tests, study design, and adverse events.
people_personalities|The Participant's Design Voice|How did user priorities shape a research system?|Use consented interviews and documented design changes.
major_events|A Clinical Study Milestone|What was actually tested, approved, and reported?|Distinguish recruitment, feasibility, clinical result, and product availability.
how_it_works|BCI for One Communication Task|How do neural signals, decoder, interface, and feedback work together?|Name device, participant population, and task.
rise_fall|A BCI Approach Changes|What evidence drove redesign or discontinuation?|Compare longitudinal performance, burdens, and alternatives.
then_vs_now|A Task Across BCI Generations|Did speed, accuracy, comfort, or independent use change?|Compare matched tasks and participant context.
future_developments|A Proposed BCI Capability|What clinical and real-world evidence would support it?|Separate laboratory demonstration from sustained benefit.
myths_vs_facts|BCI Reads Any Thought?|What signal and task was the decoder actually trained to recognize?|Explain narrow inference and uncertainty.
documentary_stories|A User's Long-Term BCI Experience|How does the system fit daily life beyond a laboratory session?|Use consented account, maintenance, support, and outcomes.
system_boundary|Brain, Decoder, and Device|Which actions are user-driven, inferred, automated, or caregiver-assisted?|Draw the actual control boundary.
input_output_trace|An Attempted Selection to Output|What neural input produced a screen or device action?|Use study data with participant privacy protection.
design_tradeoff|Implant and External Interface|How do invasiveness, signal quality, maintenance, and access compare?|Use defined devices and clinical context without treatment advice.
failure_mode|A Misinterpreted Command|How does a system detect, correct, and limit an unwanted action?|Review controlled tests and user experience.
testing_limits|A Small Study's Reach|Which populations, tasks, and durations were outside the evidence?|Report sample, follow-up, missing data, and adverse events.
standards_interoperability|BCI Device and Application Fit|Which signal, software, and assistive-device interfaces must align?|Check version and integration evidence.
security_threat_model|Neural Data and Control|Who can access signals, derived outputs, or update the decoder?|Map privacy and integrity boundaries defensively.
maintenance_lifecycle|Long-Term BCI Support|What happens when hardware, software, or research funding changes?|Check service, training, replacement, and exit plans.
infrastructure_dependencies|BCI Beyond the Sensor|Which power, computing, caregiver, and clinical support systems matter?|Map daily-use dependencies.
accessibility_usability|Control on the User's Terms|Can intended users calibrate, rest, correct errors, and opt out?|Test with participants and accessible alternatives.
independent_replication|Repeating a BCI Performance Claim|Can researchers compare results fairly?|Publish task, population, sessions, assistance, and metric definitions.
responsible_deployment|Consent and Neural Data|How are participant expectations, autonomy, data rights, and withdrawal handled?|Use approved protocols and participant voice.
field_training_or_control_data|Data That Calibrates a Decoder|Which sessions train the system and whose signals are represented?|Check consent, drift, and participant-specific limits.
field_real_world_testing|BCI at Home or in Daily Life|Does a laboratory result hold under ordinary use?|Measure task completion, setup, fatigue, support, and safety.
field_human_oversight|User and Caregiver Control|Who can pause, correct, or override an output?|Observe safe use and document authority.
field_failure_recovery|When a BCI Stops Working|How does a person communicate or act while service is unavailable?|Test fallback and support plan with users.
field_hardware_dependency|Sensor and Implant Limits|Which signal quality, durability, and service constraints define capability?|Name device version and study duration.
"""

VIRTUAL_WORLDS = """history_origins|A Shared Virtual Space Emerges|Which network and design decisions enabled one early world?|Use dated software, community, and service records.
famous_examples|A Famous Virtual World Revisited|What did participants actually create and govern?|Compare product claims with archived rules and user accounts.
hidden_stories|World Builders and Moderators|Who maintains places, tools, accessibility, and community safety?|Credit creators and consented workers.
beginner_explainers|How a Shared World Works|How do clients, servers, identities, and rendered scenes interact?|Trace one user's bounded session.
advanced_concepts|Persistent World State|What remains after participants log off and who controls it?|Examine storage, synchronization, ownership, and failure.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Disappearing Virtual Place|What records explain the loss of a world or asset?|Check service terms, moderation notices, backups, and unknowns.
technology_innovation|A New Immersive Interface|Did it improve a defined activity for intended users?|Compare comfort, accessibility, latency, and cost.
people_personalities|Community Rules in Practice|Who designed rules and resolved disputes?|Use governance records and participant perspectives.
major_events|A World Changes Hands or Shuts Down|What happened to users, creations, and records?|Build a dated service and community timeline.
how_it_works|One Multiuser Interaction|How are movements and objects synchronized across devices?|Trace network, state, and display delay.
rise_fall|Why a World Lost Users|Which evidence supports a claimed decline?|Separate active participants, accounts, sessions, and spending.
then_vs_now|A Virtual Activity Across Platforms|How did access, agency, and costs change?|Compare the same task for matched devices and users.
future_developments|A Proposed Persistent World|What must work before a promise of continuity is credible?|Test governance, export, availability, and funding.
myths_vs_facts|Virtual Ownership Equals Portability?|Can users move an asset or identity elsewhere?|Check license, format, permissions, and actual import.
documentary_stories|A Community Inside a World|How did participants build and maintain a shared place?|Use consented accounts and archival records.
system_boundary|Who Controls the World?|Where do platform, creator, moderator, and user powers meet?|Map rules, data, assets, and appeals.
input_output_trace|A User Action in Shared Space|What inputs become visible to others and what is recorded?|Trace device data, server state, and privacy.
design_tradeoff|Immersion and Accessibility|When does a headset improve presence but restrict participation?|Compare supported modes and real users.
failure_mode|A World Outage or Abuse Event|What broke and how did operators respond?|Use public postmortem or moderation record with privacy care.
testing_limits|A Demo World Versus Live Community|Which scale, device, and social conditions were excluded?|State test load and participant mix.
standards_interoperability|Avatar or Asset Across Worlds|Which file, identity, and behavior standards actually interoperate?|Test export and import on named versions.
security_threat_model|A Virtual Identity's Risks|Who can impersonate, track, or harass a participant?|Map controls and protections without abuse recipes.
maintenance_lifecycle|Keeping a World Accessible|How do software updates, moderation, backups, and hardware support affect longevity?|Review service policy and outcomes.
infrastructure_dependencies|Servers Behind a Virtual World|Which cloud, network, payments, and device services are essential?|Map outage and cost dependencies.
accessibility_usability|Participation Without One Device|Can users with different abilities join and communicate?|Test input, captions, motion settings, and alternatives.
independent_replication|Checking an Engagement Claim|Can another analyst reconstruct active use?|Publish definition, period, sampling, and exclusions.
responsible_deployment|Life Inside a Governed World|Who bears privacy, harassment, labor, and economic risks?|Consult participants and provide redress evidence.
field_software_architecture|A World Client and Server|Which services hold identity, physics, chat, and assets?|Map data and failure boundaries.
field_interface_design|A World Entry Flow|Can newcomers understand controls, rules, and consent?|Test across devices and assistive technologies.
field_version_changes|A World Update's Effects|Which objects, scripts, and users lose compatibility?|Compare release notes, migration tests, and remedies.
field_open_standards|A Portable Virtual World Claim|Are protocols and asset formats public and independently usable?|Test conformance and real cross-platform transfer.
field_technical_debt|A World Built on Old Assumptions|Which legacy format or device constraint limits change?|Trace affected creators and migration cost.
"""

DIGITAL_HUMANS = """history_origins|A Synthetic Persona Emerges|Which animation, speech, or interaction technology enabled one early example?|Use dated research and production records.
famous_examples|A Digital Human Rechecked|What was generated, scripted, recorded, or performed by a person?|Disclose production method and observed behavior.
hidden_stories|Performers Behind the Avatar|Whose face, voice, motion, or labor shaped a digital character?|Trace consent, credit, and compensation.
beginner_explainers|What Makes a Digital Human?|How do appearance, speech, behavior, and interaction combine?|Map one system and distinguish avatar from autonomous agent.
advanced_concepts|Identity and Performance Boundaries|Can a viewer tell whose expression or words they are seeing?|Examine provenance, real-time control, and disclosure.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Who Spoke Through the Avatar?|Which production records identify human, script, or model contributions?|Attribute evidence and unresolved gaps.
technology_innovation|A New Facial or Voice System|Did it improve a defined interaction without misleading users?|Test timing, comprehension, consent, and accessibility.
people_personalities|The Person Represented|How did a performer or subject control the use of their likeness?|Review agreements and consented account.
major_events|A Digital Persona Launch|What was promised and what actually worked at release?|Compare dated demo, production, and user evidence.
how_it_works|From Input to Synthetic Reply|How do speech, language, rendering, and human review create an output?|Trace a named deployment and version.
rise_fall|A Digital Character Retired|Why did a service or persona stop operating?|Check cost, audience, rights, safety, and support.
then_vs_now|One Persona Across Technology Versions|How did quality, control, and disclosure change?|Compare matched tasks and production methods.
future_developments|A Proposed Digital Human Role|What proof is needed before a system represents an organization or person?|Define autonomy, rights, error handling, and oversight.
myths_vs_facts|Looks Human, Understands Human?|Which tasks show actual comprehension and which are presentation?|Use bounded tests and failure examples.
documentary_stories|Making a Digital Character|Who recorded, designed, trained, approved, and maintained it?|Follow credited work and rights documents.
system_boundary|Human, Script, and Model|Who authors an output and who can intervene?|Draw the production and approval chain.
input_output_trace|One Digital-Human Interaction|What user data enters and what output is generated or selected?|Trace storage, model, rendering, and review.
design_tradeoff|Realism and Clear Disclosure|Does lifelike design help a task or confuse identity?|Test user understanding and comfort.
failure_mode|A Misleading Synthetic Reply|What happened when an avatar gave a wrong or unauthorized message?|Use documented incident and correction path.
testing_limits|A Polished Demo's Blind Spots|Which accents, questions, devices, and users were excluded?|Specify trials, interventions, and error rates.
standards_interoperability|Moving an Avatar|Which rig, animation, and identity formats survive transfer?|Test named tools and permissions.
security_threat_model|Misuse of Likeness and Voice|Who can produce unauthorized impersonation?|Map consent, access, provenance, and redress defensively.
maintenance_lifecycle|A Persona Over Time|How are scripts, models, voice rights, and disclosures updated?|Check owner and retirement plan.
infrastructure_dependencies|Services Behind the Face|Which models, rendering hardware, network, and actors are needed?|Map latency and outage points.
accessibility_usability|A Digital Human for Everyone|Can users read captions, avoid audio, and identify it as synthetic?|Test intended users and alternatives.
independent_replication|Repeating an Interaction Claim|Can another evaluator reproduce the result?|Publish prompts, model version, scripts, human intervention, and metrics.
responsible_deployment|Consent for a Likeness|Who controls reuse, compensation, and removal?|Examine documented rights and affected people.
field_software_architecture|The Persona's System Stack|Which modules handle recognition, response, voice, and rendering?|Map data and decision boundaries.
field_interface_design|An Avatar's Disclosure|Can users understand who or what they are interacting with?|Test label placement, comprehension, and accessibility.
field_version_changes|A Persona Model Update|Which voice, behavior, or rights conditions changed?|Compare release, evaluation, and rollback evidence.
field_open_standards|Portable Character Assets?|Can approved files move across production tools?|Test format, licensing, and fidelity.
field_technical_debt|Legacy Avatar Assets|Which old rig, script, or contract blocks updates?|Trace migration effort and rights review.
"""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("333", "333_brain-computer_interfaces", BCI,
                  "Brain-computer interfaces as defined neural signal systems for assistive communication or control, evaluated with participant autonomy, clinical evidence, privacy, and long-term support.",
                  "FDA device-study guidance, peer-reviewed methods and results, clinical study records, device documentation, and consented participant accounts",
                  "Name device, study, population, task, and follow-up. Separate laboratory feasibility from clinical benefit and never imply individual medical suitability.")
    revise_domain("334", "334_virtual_worlds", VIRTUAL_WORLDS,
                  "Virtual worlds as shared software spaces with governance, creators, identities, economies, accessibility, and persistence limits.",
                  "dated platform documentation, W3C immersive-web work, user research, moderation and governance records, and controlled usability tests",
                  "Name platform, version, device, and community. Distinguish ownership claims from contractual rights and demonstrated portability.")
    revise_domain("335", "335_digital_humans", DIGITAL_HUMANS,
                  "Digital humans as produced or interactive synthetic personas, with human performance, model behavior, likeness rights, disclosure, and audience understanding.",
                  "production records, rights agreements, system documentation, NIST synthetic-content research, and user comprehension tests",
                  "Disclose human, scripted, and generated contributions; protect likeness and voice rights and avoid treating realism as intelligence.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
